boong"],["student card","der Studentenausweis","dair shtoo-DEN-ten-ows-vice"]]},{"id":"school-verbs","title":"School verbs","items":[["to study","lernen / studieren","LAIR-nen / shtoo-DEE-ren"],["to teach","unterrichten","oon-ter-RIKH-ten"],["to ask","fragen","FRAH-gen"],["to answer","antworten","AHNT-vor-ten"],["to repeat","wiederholen","VEE-der-hoh-len"],["to understand","verstehen","fair-SHTAY-en"],["to remember","sich erinnern","zikh air-IN-ern"],["to forget","vergessen","fair-GES-en"],["to explain","erklären","air-KLAIR-en"],["to practise","üben","Ü-ben"],["to pass an exam","eine Prüfung bestehen","I-neh PRÜ-foong beh-SHTAY-en"],["to fail an exam","durch eine Prüfung fallen","doorkh I-neh PRÜ-foong FAH-len"],["to write down","aufschreiben","OWF-shri-ben"],["to listen","zuhören","TSOO-hö-ren"],["to read aloud","laut vorlesen","lowt FOR-lay-zen"],["to think","denken","DEN-ken"],["to count","zählen","TSAY-len"],["to spell","buchstabieren","bookh-shtah-BEE-ren"],["to translate","übersetzen","ü-ber-ZET-sen"],["to graduate","seinen Abschluss machen","ZI-nen AHP-shloos MAH-khen"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Ich, du, er/sie/es, wir, ihr, sie, and the polite Sie. Sie (capital S) is formal and works for one or many people."],"rows":[["I","ich","ikh"],["you (informal)","du","doo"],["he / she / it","er / sie / es","air / zee / es"],["we","wir","veer"],["you all (informal)","ihr","eer"],["they","sie","zee"],["you (formal)","Sie","zee"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ich bin Student","ikh bin shtoo-DENT"],["you are tall","du bist groß","doo bist grohs"],["she is my sister","sie ist meine Schwester","zee ist MY-neh SHVES-ter"],["we are friends","wir sind Freunde","veer zint FROYN-deh"],["they are teachers","sie sind Lehrer","zee zint LAY-rer"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Plurals are irregular. Learn each noun with its plural. The plural article is always \"die\". Common endings: -e, -en, -er, umlaut, -s, or no change."],"rows":[["der / die / das (plural)","die","dee"],["add -e (often with umlaut)","der Hund → die Hunde","doon-deh"],["add -en","die Frau → die Frauen","FROW-en"],["umlaut, no ending","der Vater → die Väter","FAY-ter"],["add -s (foreign words)","das Auto → die Autos","OW-tohs"]],"ex":[["one dog, two dogs","ein Hund, zwei Hunde","eyn hoont tsvy HOON-deh"],["one woman, women","eine Frau, Frauen","EYE-neh frow FROW-en"],["one book, two books","ein Buch, zwei Bücher","eyn bookh tsvy BEW-kher"],["one car, cars","ein Auto, Autos","eyn OW-toh OW-tohs"],["one child, children","ein Kind, Kinder","eyn kint KIN-der"]]},{"id":"sein-to-be","title":"Sein: to be","text":[],"rows":[["I am","ich bin","ikh bin"],["you are","du bist","doo bist"],["he / she is","er / sie ist","air / zee ist"],["we are","wir sind","veer zint"],["you all are","ihr seid","eer zide"],["they are / you are (formal)","sie sind / Sie sind","zee zint"]],"ex":[["I am English","ich bin Engländer","ikh bin ENG-len-der"],["he is a doctor","er ist Arzt","air ist ahrtst"],["we are tired","wir sind müde","veer zint MEW-deh"],["are you from Berlin?","bist du aus Berlin?","bist doo ows bair-LEEN"],["they are at home","sie sind zu Hause","zee zint tsoo HOW-zeh"]]},{"id":"haben-to-have","title":"Haben: to have","text":[],"rows":[["I have","ich habe","ikh HAH-beh"],["you have","du hast","doo hahst"],["he / she has","er / sie hat","air / zee haht"],["we have","wir haben","veer HAH-ben"],["you all have","ihr habt","eer hahpt"],["they have","sie haben","zee HAH-ben"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","ich habe einen Bruder","ikh HAH-beh EYE-nen BROO-der"],["she has two cats","sie hat zwei Katzen","zee haht tsvy KAHT-sen"],["we have time","wir haben Zeit","veer HAH-ben tsite"],["do you have a pen?","hast du einen Stift?","hahst doo EYE-nen shtift"],["they have a car","sie haben ein Auto","zee HAH-ben eyn OW-toh"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Take off -en, then add: -e, -st, -t, -en, -t, -en. Example: machen (to do)."],"rows":[["ich","mache","MAH-kheh"],["du","machst","mahkhst"],["er / sie / es","macht","mahkht"],["wir","machen","MAH-khen"],["ihr","macht","mahkht"],["sie / Sie","machen","MAH-khen"]],"ex":[["I live in Berlin","ich wohne in Berlin","ikh VOH-neh in bair-LEEN"],["you work a lot","du arbeitest viel","doo AR-by-test feel"],["she plays football","sie spielt Fußball","zee shpeelt FOOS-bahl"],["we learn German","wir lernen Deutsch","veer LAIR-nen doytsh"],["they buy bread","sie kaufen Brot","zee KOW-fen broht"]]},{"id":"gehen-to-go","title":"Gehen: to go","text":["Going to do something soon: use gehen or the future. Ich gehe schlafen = I am going to sleep."],"rows":[["I go","ich gehe","ikh GAY-eh"],["you go","du gehst","doo gayst"],["he / she goes","er / sie geht","air / zee gayt"],["we go","wir gehen","veer GAY-en"],["they go","sie gehen","zee GAY-en"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","ich gehe zur Schule","ikh GAY-eh tsoor SHOO-leh"],["where are you going?","wohin gehst du?","voh-HIN gayst doo"],["we are going home","wir gehen nach Hause","veer GAY-en nahkh HOW-zeh"],["she is going shopping","sie geht einkaufen","zee gayt EYN-kow-fen"],["let's go!","los geht's!","lohs gayts"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb is always in position 2. Subject, verb, rest. If you start with time or place, the verb stays second, and the subject moves after it."],"rows":[["subject + verb + rest","Ich esse Brot.","ikh ES-eh broht"],["time first","Heute esse ich Brot.","HOY-teh ES-eh ikh broht"],["with a second verb at the end","Ich will Brot essen.","ikh vil broht ES-en"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","ich esse Brot","ikh ES-eh broht"],["today I eat bread","heute esse ich Brot","HOY-teh ES-eh ikh broht"],["I want to eat bread","ich will Brot essen","ikh vil broht ES-en"],["he lives here","er wohnt hier","air vohnt heer"],["we go to school today","wir gehen heute zur Schule","veer GAY-en HOY-teh tsoor SHOO-leh"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Use nicht (not) for verbs and adjectives. Use kein (no / not a) for nouns.","nicht negates verbs, adjectives and adverbs (ich arbeite nicht). kein negates a noun that has \"ein\" or no article (ich habe kein Auto). Also: nichts (nothing), niemand (nobody), nie (never)."],"rows":[["not (verb, adjective)","nicht","nikht"],["not a, no","kein / keine","kine / KY-neh"],["nothing","nichts","nikhts"],["nobody","niemand","NEE-mahnt"],["never","nie","nee"],["not","nicht","nikht"],["no / not a","kein","kine"],["nothing","nichts","nikhts"],["nobody","niemand","NEE-mahnt"],["never","nie","nee"]],"ex":[["I want","ich will","ikh vil"],["I do not want","ich will nicht","ikh vil nikht"],["I speak English","ich spreche Englisch","ikh SHPREKH-eh ENG-lish"],["I do not speak English","ich spreche kein Englisch","ikh SHPREKH-eh kine ENG-lish"],["I like it","es gefällt mir","es geh-FELT meer"],["I do not like it","es gefällt mir nicht","es geh-FELT meer nikht"],["she is here","sie ist hier","zee ist heer"],["she is not here","sie ist nicht hier","zee ist nikht heer"],["I have a car","ich habe ein Auto","ikh HAH-beh ine OW-toh"],["I do not have a car","ich habe kein Auto","ikh HAH-beh kine OW-toh"],["I understand","ich verstehe","ikh fair-SHTAY-eh"],["I do not understand","ich verstehe nicht","ikh fair-SHTAY-eh nikht"],["we are tired","wir sind müde","veer zint MÜ-deh"],["we are not tired","wir sind nicht müde","veer zint nikht MÜ-deh"],["he works on Sundays","er arbeitet sonntags","air AR-bi-tet ZON-tahgs"],["he does not work on Sundays","er arbeitet sonntags nicht","air AR-bi-tet ZON-tahgs nikht"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Yes or no question: put the verb first. With a question word: question word, then verb, then subject."],"rows":[["statement","Du sprichst Englisch.","doo shprikhst ENG-lish"],["question","Sprichst du Englisch?","shprikhst doo ENG-lish"],["with question word","Wo wohnst du?","voh vohnst doo"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","sprichst du Englisch?","shprikhst doo ENG-lish"],["is she a doctor?","ist sie Ärztin?","ist zee AIRTS-tin"],["do you have a pen?","hast du einen Stift?","hahst doo EYE-nen shtift"],["are you tired?","bist du müde?","bist doo MEW-deh"],["is it far?","ist es weit?","ist es vite"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","was","vahs"],["who","wer","vair"],["where","wo","voh"],["where to","wohin","voh-HIN"],["where from","woher","voh-HAIR"],["when","wann","vahn"],["why","warum","vah-ROOM"],["how","wie","vee"],["which","welcher","VEL-kher"],["how much / how many","wie viel / wie viele","vee feel / vee FEE-leh"]],"ex":[["what is this?","was ist das?","vahs ist dahs"],["who is she?","wer ist sie?","vair ist zee"],["where do you live?","wo wohnst du?","voh vohnst doo"],["when is the exam?","wann ist die Prüfung?","vahn ist dee PREW-foong"],["why are you late?","warum bist du spät?","vah-ROOM bist doo shpayt"],["how much is it?","wie viel kostet das?","vee feel KOS-tet dahs"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":[],"rows":[["my","mein / meine","mine / MY-neh"],["your (informal)","dein / deine","dine / DY-neh"],["his / its","sein / seine","zine / ZY-neh"],["her","ihr / ihre","eer / EER-eh"],["our","unser / unsere","OON-zer / OON-zer-eh"],["your (formal)","Ihr / Ihre","eer / EER-eh"]],"ex":[["my house","mein Haus","mine hows"],["your friends","deine Freunde","DY-neh FROYN-deh"],["his sister","seine Schwester","ZY-neh SHVES-ter"],["our teacher","unser Lehrer","OON-zer LAY-rer"],["your name (formal)","Ihr Name","eer NAH-meh"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["du / dein / dir for friends. Sie / Ihr / Ihnen for strangers. With Sie, the verb is the same as \"they\" (sie ... -en)."],"rows":[["you, informal","du","doo"],["you, formal","Sie","zee"],["your, informal","dein","dine"],["your, formal","Ihr","eer"],["to you, formal","Ihnen","EE-nen"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","du sprichst","doo shprikhst"],["you speak (formal)","Sie sprechen","zee SHPREKH-en"],["how are you? (informal)","wie geht's dir?","vee gayts deer"],["how are you? (formal)","wie geht es Ihnen?","vee gayt es EE-nen"],["thank you (formal)","vielen Dank, Herr Müller","FEE-len dahnk hair MEW-ler"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Spoken past: haben / sein + past participle (ge-...-t or ge-...-en). Future: werden + infinitive."],"rows":[["I have worked","ich habe gearbeitet","ikh HAH-beh geh-AR-by-tet"],["I have eaten","ich habe gegessen","ikh HAH-beh geh-GES-en"],["I went","ich bin gegangen","ikh bin geh-GAHNG-en"],["I will go","ich werde gehen","ikh VAIR-deh GAY-en"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","gestern habe ich gearbeitet","GES-tern HAH-beh ikh geh-AR-by-tet"],["she bought a book","sie hat ein Buch gekauft","zee haht eyn bookh geh-KOWFT"],["I went home","ich bin nach Hause gegangen","ikh bin nahkh HOW-zeh geh-GAHNG-en"],["I will call you tomorrow","ich rufe dich morgen an","ikh ROO-feh dikh MOR-gen ahn"],["we will eat at eight","wir essen um acht Uhr","veer ES-en oom ahkht oor"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal (du): verb stem, no ending (komm!, geh!). Plural (ihr): -t (kommt!). Formal (Sie): infinitive + Sie (kommen Sie!). Negative: add nicht (komm nicht!)."],"rows":[["come! (du)","komm!","kom"],["come! (ihr)","kommt!","komt"],["come! (formal)","kommen Sie!","KOM-en zee"]],"ex":[["come here","komm her","kom hair"],["do not come here","komm nicht her","kom nikht hair"],["sit down","setz dich","zets dikh"],["do not sit down","setz dich nicht","zets dikh nikht"],["be quiet","sei still","zi shtil"],["do not be late","komm nicht zu spät","kom nikht tsoo shpayt"],["open the door","mach die Tür auf","makh dee tür owf"],["close the window","mach das Fenster zu","makh dahs FEN-ster tsoo"],["listen to me","hör mir zu","hör meer tsoo"],["do not worry","mach dir keine Sorgen","makh deer KI-neh ZOR-gen"],["speak slowly","sprich langsam","shprikh LAHNG-zahm"],["wait a moment","warte einen Moment","VAR-teh I-nen moh-MENT"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["können (can), müssen (must), wollen (want) + infinitive at the END: ich kann schwimmen, wir müssen gehen, ich will essen. nicht müssen = need not; nicht dürfen = must not."],"rows":[["I can","ich kann","ikh kahn"],["I must","ich muss","ikh moos"],["I want","ich will","ikh vil"]],"ex":[["I can swim","ich kann schwimmen","ikh kahn SHVIM-en"],["I cannot swim","ich kann nicht schwimmen","ikh kahn nikht SHVIM-en"],["can you help me?","kannst du mir helfen?","kahnst doo meer HEL-fen"],["we must go","wir müssen gehen","veer MÜ-sen GAY-en"],["we must not go","wir dürfen nicht gehen","veer DÜR-fen nikht GAY-en"],["I want to eat","ich will essen","ikh vil ES-en"],["I do not want to eat","ich will nicht essen","ikh vil nikht ES-en"],["you can come","du kannst kommen","doo kahnst KOM-en"],["you cannot come","du kannst nicht kommen","doo kahnst nikht KOM-en"],["she wants to study","sie will studieren","zee vil shtoo-DEE-ren"],["I must work today","ich muss heute arbeiten","ikh moos HOY-teh AR-bi-ten"],["you must not run","du darfst nicht rennen","doo dahrfst nikht REN-en"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["auf (on top of), unter (under), in (in), neben (next to), bei / in der Nähe von (near), um neun Uhr (at nine). Place words take the dative when you say where something is."],"rows":[["on","auf","owf"],["under","unter","OON-ter"],["next to","neben","NAY-ben"],["near","in der Nähe von","in dair NAY-eh fon"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","das Buch liegt auf dem Tisch","dahs bookh leekt owf daym tish"],["the cat is under the table","die Katze ist unter dem Tisch","dee KAT-seh ist OON-ter daym tish"],["I am at school","ich bin in der Schule","ikh bin in dair SHOO-leh"],["I am at home","ich bin zu Hause","ikh bin tsoo HOW-zeh"],["the shop is next to the bank","das Geschäft ist neben der Bank","dahs geh-SHEFT ist NAY-ben dair bahnk"],["the park is near the station","der Park ist in der Nähe vom Bahnhof","dair park ist in dair NAY-eh fom BAHN-hohf"],["we meet in the morning","wir treffen uns am Morgen","veer TREF-en oons ahm MOR-gen"],["the lesson is at nine","der Unterricht ist um neun Uhr","dair OON-ter-rikht ist oom noyn oor"],["the key is in the bag","der Schlüssel ist in der Tasche","dair SHLÜ-sel ist in dair TAH-sheh"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["adjective + er = comparative (groß, größer); am + adjective + sten = the most (am größten). als = than. gut, besser, am besten (good, better, best)."],"rows":[["bigger than","größer als","GRÖ-ser ahls"],["better","besser","BES-er"],["the biggest","am größten","ahm GRÖ-sten"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","groß, größer, am größten","grohs GRÖ-ser ahm GRÖ-sten"],["small, smaller, the smallest","klein, kleiner, am kleinsten","kline KLI-ner ahm KLINE-sten"],["this is better than that","das ist besser als das","dahs ist BES-er ahls dahs"],["this is worse than that","das ist schlechter als das","dahs ist SHLEKH-ter ahls dahs"],["she is taller than me","sie ist größer als ich","zee ist GRÖ-ser ahls ikh"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Taschkent ist größer als Samarkand","tahsh-KENT ist GRÖ-ser ahls zah-mar-KAHNT"],["it is the cheapest","es ist am billigsten","es ist ahm BIL-ikh-sten"],["the same as","genauso wie","geh-NOW-zoh vee"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","er ist Lehrer","air ist LAIR-er"],["you (plural) are students","ihr seid Schüler","eer zite SHÜ-ler"],["I am happy","ich bin glücklich","ikh bin GLÜK-likh"],["she is at school","sie ist in der Schule","zee ist in dair SHOO-leh"],["you are my friend","du bist mein Freund","doo bist mine froynt"],["it is cold","es ist kalt","es ist kahlt"],["I study English","ich lerne Englisch","ikh LAIR-neh ENG-lish"],["he teaches maths","er unterrichtet Mathe","air oon-ter-RIKH-tet MAH-teh"],["they work every day","sie arbeiten jeden Tag","zee AR-bi-ten YAY-den tahg"],["is this your book?","ist das dein Buch?","ist dahs dine bookh"],["are they here?","sind sie hier?","zint zee heer"],["do you like tea?","magst du Tee?","mahgst doo tay"],["what time is it?","wie spät ist es?","vee shpayt ist es"],["whose book is this?","wessen Buch ist das?","VES-en bookh ist dahs"],["how old are you?","wie alt bist du?","vee ahlt bist doo"],["how do you say it?","wie sagt man das?","vee zahgt mahn dahs"],["your book (formal)","Ihr Buch","eer bookh"],["their house","ihr Haus","eer hows"],["my phone","mein Handy","mine HEN-dee"],["excuse me, sir","entschuldigen Sie, mein Herr","ent-SHOOL-dee-gen zee mine hair"],["please sit down (formal)","bitte setzen Sie sich","BIT-teh ZET-sen zee zikh"],["come here (informal)","komm her","kom hair"],["yesterday I was tired","gestern war ich müde","GES-tern var ikh MÜ-deh"],["I will study tomorrow","ich werde morgen lernen","ikh VAIR-deh MOR-gen LAIR-nen"],["we went to the park","wir sind in den Park gegangen","veer zint in dayn park geh-GAHNG-en"]]}],"name":"German","id":"de","flag":"de","note":""}